<title>USA: RedFed supervisory pact ended.</title>
<headline>RedFed supervisory pact ended.</headline>
<dateline>REDLANDS, Calif. 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>RedFed Bancorp Inc, the holding company for Redlands Federal Bank, said on Monday the Office of Thrift Supervision had terminated the Supervisory Agreement which had been entered into on April 25, 1995.</p>
<p>RedFed Bancorp said in a statement it recently completed a 2.6-million-share secondary stock offering. The offering placed the bank in the &quot;well capitalized&quot; category of institutions under Office of Thrift Supervision regulations.</p>
<p>The bank's tangible and core capital ratios increased to 8.02 percent as of August 19 and its risk-based capital ratio increased to 11.81 percent.</p>
<p>-- New York newsroom, (212) 859-1610</p>
